"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_010_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "10", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/14"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_011_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "11", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/15"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/16"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "17", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/17"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "18", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/18"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "19", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/19"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "20", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/20"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "21", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/21"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_018_thumb.jpg", "page": "22", "label": "18", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/22"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_019_thumb.jpg", "page": "23", "label": "[19]", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/23"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_020_thumb.jpg", "page": "24", "label": "[20]", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/24"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "ordinance-14-november-1842", "series": "JSPPA", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPA6", "documentSeriesIdCompiled": "jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-421114", "documentSeriesUri": "/the-papers/administrative-records/jsppa6/jsppa6-sub-nccr/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-421114", "documentSeriesTitle": "<p>\r\n\tMeeting, 14 November 1842</p>", "editorialPageNumber": "6", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/54016763/54016763-0010.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> it, that thereby material facts may be ascertained. The said Court shall proceed in a summary way to settle the said facts, by hearing the testimony &amp; arguments, as well of all Parties interested civilly, if any there be, as of the Prisoner, or Prisoners and the Person or Persons who holds him her or them in custody, and shall dispose of the Prisoner or Prisoners as the case may require. If it appear that the prisoner or Prisoners are in custody by virtue of Process from any Court, legally constituted, he she or they can be discharged for the following causes: first, where the Court has exceeded the limits of its jurisdicton, either as to the matter, place, Sum, Person or Persons; second, where though the Original imprisonment was lawful, yet by some Act, Omission, or event, which has subsequently taken place, the party has become entitled to his her or their discharge; third, where the process is defective in some substantial form required by law; fourth where the process though in proper form has been issued in a Case [p. 6]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> it, that thereby material facts may be ascertained. The <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>said Court shall proceed in a summary way to settle the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>said facts, by hearing the testimony &amp; arguments, as well of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>all Parties interested civilly, if any there be, as of the Prisoner, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>&lt;​or Prisoners​&gt; and the Person &lt;​or Persons​&gt; who holds him &lt;​her​&gt; or <span class=\"deleted\">her</span> &lt;​them​&gt; in custody, and shall <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>dispose of the Prisoner &lt;​or Prisoners​&gt; as the case may require. If it <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>appear that the prisoner &lt;​or Prisoners​&gt; <span class=\"deleted\">is</span> &lt;​are​&gt; in custody by virtue of Process <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>from any Court, legally constituted, he &lt;​she or they​&gt; can be discharged <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>for the following causes: first, where the Court has exceeded <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the limits of its jurisdicton, either as to the matter, place, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Sum, &lt;​Person​&gt; or Persons; second, where though the Original impri<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>sonment was lawful, yet by some Act, Omission, or event, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>which has subsequently taken place, the party has become <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>entitled to his &lt;​her or their​&gt; discharge; third, where the process is defective <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>in some substantial form required by law; fourth where <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the process though in proper form has been issued in a Case [p. 6]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "Nauvoo City Council Minute Book, 1841–1845", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/nauvoo-city-council-minute-book-1841-1845/125", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "Ordinance, 14 Nove